WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.220
Bran Stark: The Starks of Winterfell trace
their descent to the First Men in the Age

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.320
of Heroes.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:10.330
The family's founder was Brandon the Builder
who, in the aftermath of the Long Night, helped

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:14.250
establish the Night's Watch.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:18.370
Legend has it, he enlisted the aid of giants
and the powerful magic of the Children of

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:23.660
the Forest to raise the mighty Wall, which
has protected the realm for generations.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.470
He went on to build the ancestral seat of
Winterfell and reigned as the first King in

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.740
the North.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.300
The Starks take great pride in their history
and traditions.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:39.010
It is one of the few noble houses that still
keeps the Old Gods; a sacred weirwood lives

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.420
large in Winterfell's godswood.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:50.039
Its ancestral sword, Ice, was forged in ancient
Valyria and passed down through the generations.

00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:55.420
House Stark remains steadfast in its support
of the Night's Watch, even as the once illustrious

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.809
order has fallen on hard times.

00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:03.269
Much like their sigil, the grey direwolf,
House Stark is the stuff of legend in the

00:01:03.269 --> 00:01:05.750
North and throughout the Seven Kingdoms...

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:11.030
Bran and Robb Stark: ... and their family
words, "Winter Is Coming" serve as a reminder

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:12.030
of their beginnings...

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:16.100
Robb Stark: ... in the wake of the Long Night
and a grim portent of things to come.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:21.730
Roose Bolton: Like the Starks, the blood of
House Bolton runs back to the First Men.

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:24.180
Singers call those times the "Age of Heroes."

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:30.140
A mask for a savage world that bred savage
men.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:35.220
The Lannisters swindled their enemies, the
Storm Kings hammered them, and the Starks

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.970
cut off their heads.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:44.880
In such company as this, were the Boltons
really so indelicate?

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:51.130
Unlike some other houses, my ancestors earned
the Bolton words, "Our blades are sharp."

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:57.730
They passed down not a Valyriangreatsword
but a knife honed and thin enough to fit between

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:02.820
the topmost layer of skin and the tissue below
and peel.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:11.989
For as we all learned as children, a naked
man has few secrets; a flayed man, none.

00:02:11.989 --> 00:02:18.769
In those dark days, they say some of my more
wilfulforebearers would even wear their enemies'

00:02:18.769 --> 00:02:20.489
skins as cloaks.

00:02:20.489 --> 00:02:24.430
But no such tokens remain if they ever existed.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:32.019
Certainly not hanging in some secret room
in the Dreadfort, as old wives and fools insist.

00:02:32.019 --> 00:02:38.650
I suspect my House itself was responsible
for spreading such rumors in the first place.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:43.769
Few weapons are as effective as terror, and
this was an age of war.

00:02:43.769 --> 00:02:47.900
House against House, brother against brother.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:52.359
The ironmen were on the rise and never far
from our shores.

00:02:52.359 --> 00:02:57.060
We must have seemed ripe for the taking, too
busy fighting each other to deal with the

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.749
raiders as they deserved.

00:02:59.749 --> 00:03:06.530
Thus the Starks took it upon themselves to
unify the North under them.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:11.609
They drove the pirates out of White Knife
and claimed the eastern coast and married

00:03:11.609 --> 00:03:13.980
the Marsh King's daughter for the Neck.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:20.299
A Stark wrestled for Bear Island and won,
or so they say.

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:21.299
Silly stories.

00:03:21.299 --> 00:03:25.779
Blood and steel won the North, and the Starks
had the most of both.

00:03:25.779 --> 00:03:31.359
Sansa Stark: With most of the South in Aegon's
hands, the best chance to throw back the Conqueror

00:03:31.359 --> 00:03:35.659
now lay with the North, if we cared enough
to try.

00:03:35.659 --> 00:03:39.980
Unlike our southern rivals, the Stark Kings
of Winter didn't forge the North into one

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:46.379
kingdom for glory or gold (there is little
of either here), but to survive.

00:03:46.379 --> 00:03:52.249
Alone in Westeros, the North remembered when
worse than dragons lay waste to armies.

00:03:52.249 --> 00:03:57.830
Thousands of years ago, the sun set on the
realms of men, and the Long Night began.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:01.989
A new race emerged from the ice and snow:
the White Walkers.

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:07.700
They demanded no crown, offered no terms,
spared no life, and the dead marched with

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:08.700
them.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:14.309
With humanity facing extinction, a Stark sought
out the Children of the Forest, the most ancient

00:04:14.309 --> 00:04:19.299
beings in Westeros, and convinced them to
ally with the men they'd once fought.

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:24.840
Together, the two races pushed the Walkers
back into the Land of Always Winter and sealed

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:31.310
it off from the Seven Kingdoms with the Wall,
three hundred miles of ice, stone, and earth

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.509
rising nearly seven hundred feet tall.

00:04:33.509 --> 00:04:39.030
To guard it, they established the Night's
Watch, a brotherhood sworn to defend the living

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:42.600
from the dead, whose vows erase both titles
and crimes.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:48.740
Viserys Targaryen: After the Long Night, the
North tried to forget it belonged to a continent.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:51.750
Perhaps through pride, perhaps through sheer
ignorance.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.720
You never can tell with the North.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:05:00.990
But as news of Aegon's dragons spread, Torrhen
Stark, the King of Winter, knew he couldn't

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:06.490
forget Westeros any longer and summoned his
lords to Winterfell.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:11.460
Many fools shrugged off the threat while the
rest placed wages on how long the South would

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:12.930
take to burn.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:18.800
Torrhen silenced them with a command to assemble
their armies and descend from the North in

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:19.800
force.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:25.090
Sansa: As the kings of the Rock and the Reach
burned on the Field of Fire, the greatest

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:29.260
Northern force since the Long Night crossed
the Neck into the Riverlands.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:35.230
But when King Torrhen arrived at the Trident,
he saw on the opposing riverbank the combined

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:38.199
strength of all Aegon's conquered kingdoms.

00:05:38.199 --> 00:05:44.240
A force larger than Torrhen's own by half,
and with three dragons.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:50.110
Viserys: That night, King Torrhen called a
conference of all his lords and advisors.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:56.930
Some wanted to fight and trust Northern valor
to carry the day (and burn on the Trident).

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:02.169
The wisest of them wanted to withdraw to Moat
Cailin, the fortress which had thrown back

00:06:02.169 --> 00:06:06.060
every southern invasion (and burn there).

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:12.979
One suicidal lord even wanted to ambush Aegon's
camp in the dark and kill the dragons as they

00:06:12.979 --> 00:06:15.760
slept or at the very least, their riders.

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:19.330
Hard to tell what would have been his fate.

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:20.379
Burning?

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:21.419
Beheading?

00:06:21.419 --> 00:06:24.560
Dismemberment?Perhaps all three.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:29.879
Sansa: My ancestor listened to their counsel,
and, in the morning, crossed the Trident under

00:06:29.879 --> 00:06:31.770
a flag of parley.

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:36.970
Then King Torrhen of House Stark laid his
ancient crown at Aegon's feet and was named

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:40.210
Lord of Winterfell and Warden of the North.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.280
Viserys: And the King Who Knelt.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:48.349
Sansa: He had no choice, and thanks to him,
our soldiers returned to their homes whole

00:06:48.349 --> 00:06:50.319
and unharmed.

00:06:50.319 --> 00:06:54.669
The swords that Aegon took from them were
not twisted, burnt, or mangled.

00:06:54.669 --> 00:06:55.940
Viserys: Yet.

00:06:55.940 --> 00:07:02.300
Barristan Selmy:Then came Lord Whent's tourney
at Harrenhal, the largest ever in Westeros.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:07.440
I unhorsed every man against me until only
Prince Rhaegar remained.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:14.710
We each set our feet in our saddles and lowered
our lances and charged, and I fell.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:18.940
Muddy and bruised, I then watched Rhaegar
present Lyanna Stark with the victor's crown

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:24.630
of roses, though she was betrothed to Robert
Baratheon and Rhaegar himself was married

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.389
to Elia Martell.

00:07:26.389 --> 00:07:27.870
We all know what happened after.

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:32.930
If I had I been a bit quicker with my lance,
had I chosen a faster horse, perhaps I could

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:35.889
have spared the kingdom from the destruction
that came after.

00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:40.990
Or if I had thought to warn Brandon Stark
against his rashness.

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:44.970
He came to King's Landing himself demanding
Rhaegar return his sister.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:45.970
Poor fool.

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:52.210
If he had only known the depth of Aerys' madness,
he wouldn't have dared provoke him.

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:56.770
Aerys ordered Brandon imprisoned, while I
could do nothing but obey.

00:07:56.770 --> 00:08:01.919
When Brandon's father, Lord Rickard Stark,
came to King's Landing to beg for his son,

00:08:01.919 --> 00:08:05.879
Aerys burned him alive, while I could do nothing
but watch.

00:08:05.879 --> 00:08:14.840
I had sworn a vow to a mad king and was honor-bound
to obey him, even at the cost of my soul.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:18.870
Varys: We urged Aerys to pardon Brandon Stark.

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:23.780
The boy had threatened Prince Rhaegar, but
Rhaegar had stolen the boy's sister, and the

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:27.120
boy was the eldest son of our Warden of the
North.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:32.729
Baelish: Who is the greater fool: a mad king
or the man who reasons with him?

00:08:32.729 --> 00:08:35.729
Aerys saw knives in every shadow.

00:08:35.729 --> 00:08:41.349
When you told him to treat the Starks with
caution, you made him afraid and what he feared

00:08:41.349 --> 00:08:42.349
he killed.

00:08:42.349 --> 00:08:46.570
Varys: I wouldn't have thought you of all
people would bother with recriminations for

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:49.130
Brandon's death, Lord Baelish.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:52.790
Not after your, shall we call it, "duel" with
him?

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:59.290
Baelish: Brandon was as arrogant as he was
stupid; like his father, Lord Stark, who answered

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:01.089
Aerys' summon to the capital.

00:09:01.089 --> 00:09:03.510
They earned their fates.

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:07.500
But the younger son, Ned, what was his crime?

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.700
That Aerys ordered his death as well?

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:14.420
Varys: Unlike men, families do not die when
you lop off their head.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:17.690
Baelish: When did you know you'd lost, Lord
Varys?

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:21.889
Varys: When Robert Baratheon killed Prince
Rhaegar on the Trident.

00:09:21.889 --> 00:09:23.600
Baelish: Wrong.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.950
You lost the war when you let Ned Stark slip
back into the North.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:32.700
Neither the Bloody Gate of the Vale or Moat
Cailin in the North have ever fallen.

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:38.029
They could have held out for years even if
you'd killed Robert, but you let him slip

00:09:38.029 --> 00:09:39.900
through your fingers as well.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:44.421
Varys: I told the court that Robert was hiding
in the Stoney Sept, but the Hand of the King

00:09:44.421 --> 00:09:47.950
wasted too much time searching the city.

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:51.329
Something about the glory of single combat.

00:09:51.329 --> 00:09:54.920
Then Ned Stark's army arrived to save the
day.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:10:01.120
Catelyn Stark:Robert won and my husband avenged
his brother and my love.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:07.600
But when he came home to me, he could not
meet my eyes.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:11.980
I saw the reason by his side.

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:17.690
Many men have bastards, I know, and under
the strain of war, any man, no matter how

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:23.260
honorable, may forsake his vows for a night
of warmth that he may never know again.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:27.060
But Ned Stark was not built like other men.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:33.910
His northern honor would not let him sequester
his shame in some distant holdfast.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:42.510
He brought this boy, this "Jon Snow," home
to raise with his trueborn children.

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:43.650
My children.

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:49.910
The Starks are of the North, and, like the
snows of winter, when they come south, they

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:51.129
melt away.

